Manage-all clients permission no longer implies view-all

A resource-type MANAGE grant lets an admin create/delete clients via canManage(), but canView() only checks VIEW. That means the same admin cannot list or view all clients, unlike per-client manage (canView(client) delegates through canConfigure/canManage) and the existing admin-role semantics where manage-clients includes view-clients. This also contradicts the interface contract for ClientScopeModel view, which documents VIEW or MANAGE. Include MANAGE in the global view check.

Proposed patch:
```diff
--- a/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java
+++ b/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ public class ClientPermissionsV2 extends ClientPermissions {

     @Override
     public boolean canView() {
-        return canViewClientDefault() || hasPermission(AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW);
+        return canViewClientDefault() || hasPermission(AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW) || hasPermission(AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE);
     }

     @Override

```

