Return group ids, not authz resource ids

`getGroupIdsWithViewPermission()` feeds its result into `UserModel.GROUPS`, and `JpaUserProvider` compares those values to `UserGroupMembershipEntity.groupId`. The new V2 implementation adds `groupResource.getId()`, which is the authorization resource id, not the Keycloak group id. That makes user searches/counts return no members for group-scoped `view-members`/`manage-members` permissions. V2 group resources are named with the group id, so use the resource name for both the permission check and returned set.

Proposed patch:
```diff
--- a/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/GroupPermissionsV2.java
+++ b/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/GroupPermissionsV2.java
@@ -109,9 +109,9 @@ class GroupPermissionsV2 extends GroupPermissions {
         Set<String> granted = new HashSet<>();

         resourceStore.findByType(server, AdminPermissionsSchema.GROUPS_RESOURCE_TYPE, groupResource -> {
-            if (hasPermission(groupResource.getId(), AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW_MEMBERS, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE_MEMBERS)) {
-                granted.add(groupResource.getId());
+            if (hasPermission(groupResource.getName(), AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW_MEMBERS, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE_MEMBERS)) {
+                granted.add(groupResource.getName());
             }
         });

         return granted;

```

