Handle missing all-users resource

If a user-specific resource is absent, this falls back to the all-users resource and then calls `policyStore.findByResource(server, resource)` without checking whether the type resource exists. For a realm/admin-permissions client that has not yet initialized the Users resource type resource, this turns a simple authorization denial into a NullPointerException. Guard the null fallback before querying policies.

Proposed patch:
```diff
--- a/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/UserPermissionsV2.java
+++ b/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/UserPermissionsV2.java
@@ -105,6 +105,10 @@ class UserPermissionsV2 extends UserPermissions {
             // check if there is permission for "all-users". If so, load its resource and proceed with evaluation
             resource = AdminPermissionsSchema.SCHEMA.getResourceTypeResource(session, server, AdminPermissionsSchema.USERS_RESOURCE_TYPE);

+            if (resource == null) {
+                return false;
+            }
+
             if (policyStore.findByResource(server, resource).isEmpty()) {
                 return false;
             }

