Access token matcher rejects the expected grant

The new matcher currently returns false when the extracted shortcut equals the expected shortcut, so all event expectations using `isAccessTokenId(...)` fail for correctly encoded token IDs. The grant shortcut is also encoded in positions 4-5 of the six-character prefix (after 2 chars session type and 2 chars token type), so the substring should start at index 4 and be negated. Adding a prefix length check avoids `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException` for malformed values.

Proposed patch:
```diff
--- a/testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/AssertEvents.java
+++ b/testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/AssertEvents.java
@@ -478,6 +478,7 @@ public class AssertEvents implements TestRule {
                 String[] items = item.split(":");
                 if (items.length != 2) return false;
                 // Grant type shortcut starts at character 4th char and is 2-chars long
-                if (items[0].substring(3, 5).equals(expectedGrantShortcut)) return false;
+                if (items[0].length() != 6) return false;
+                if (!items[0].substring(4, 6).equals(expectedGrantShortcut)) return false;
                 return isUUID().matches(items[1]);
             }

```

