Salesforce connection still uses the stale access token

The new refresh path saves the refreshed Salesforce tokens, but the `jsforce.Connection` is constructed with `credentialKey.access_token` from before the refresh. If the stored token was expired, the first Salesforce request made by this service will still authenticate with the expired token despite a successful refresh. Use the refreshed token data when creating the connection.

